{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/56099-cyberpunk-changeling","id":56099,"title":"Cyberpunk Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T07:04:33-08:00","id":56099,"title":"Cyberpunk Changeling","content":"Looking for ideas, sources and inspirations. I'll start with what I found.<br /> <br /> nWoD books to steal from:<br /> - Mirrors: Bleeding Edge<br /> - Hunter the Vigil line<br /> - Demon the Descent<br /> - God Machine Chronicle<br /> <br /> other RPG books:<br /> - Kuro RPG from Cubicle7<br /> <br /> books:<br /> - Vurt series (Vurt, Pollen, Automated Alice, Nymphomation) by Jeff Noon<br /> <br /> <br /> That's all for now. I'm looking for ways to focus more on dehumanisation and alienation via high-tech vs. low-life and madness theme via use holograms and augumented reality than for example megacorps and VR. I would like to change as little as possible from original CtL stuff, only enhance it, but I'm open for any ideas. I'd rather see Arcadia as another world and Hedge as unstable dimension between them that reshape itself using thoughts of visitors, than making it a virtual reality or turning changelings into alien-implanted people. I'd like to use the hedge leaking into AR from time to time though, to emphasise madness theme. I want to keep all the weird fairy-tale magic and put it into future, not to reskin everything as alien tech.<br /> <br /> I would need more sources for high-tech stuff and magi-tech tokens and some ideas how to expand fetches. With fetches I'm much more open to even far going changes, as turning them into androids or clones. I'm looking between Demon and Promethean but can't figure anything neat and simple for now.<br /> <br /> I hope for some good brainstorming here. :]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T07:44:55-08:00","id":56116,"title":"","content":"Do androids dream of electric sheep? If so, can a changeling visit those dreams, and maybe navigate from there into computer networks using something akin to the Skein? <b>Changeling</b> is uniquely situated to do things involving cyberpunk\u2019s traditional VR by drawing parallels between the Net and the Skein: e.g., the oneiromancy rules could easily be adapted to represent netrunning by treating the VR environments as if they were \u201cdreamscapes\u201d of computer systems . Blurring the boundaries between the two is in keeping with the notion that the line between man and machine is becoming blurred. <br /> <br /> I would allow Plug-Ins that emulate most demonic form Modifications; they\u2019re already halfway to being cybernetic implants as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:49:37-08:00","id":56263,"title":"","content":"<br /> When I first heard about the God Machine ... I couldn't help but think of Arcadia as a gremlin in its gears. Or maybe Arcadia represents a different &quot;OS&quot; of a reality ... an OS that became infected with a fairy curse and is now trying to corrupt the default settings of the World of Darkness with the Wyrd Virus, which it does by putting self replicating commands in people. Every changeling infected with the Wyrd Virus begins to mutate into something else, something that reflects the strange entities that sometimes call themselves fairies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:55:19-08:00","id":56267,"title":"","content":"There's that strange story about the Fae starting out as mechanical beings, and falling to become the free beings they are....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:48:33-08:00","id":57549,"title":"","content":"Firefly Night: Pun or Gremlins from Winter Masques?<br /> <br /> Alexander: Winter masques is a good addition to your list. It has lots of backround information on what humans go through in Arcadia. And you can even find Arcadian Internet from it. Every chirurgeon goes through worse in Arcadia than normal CP streetdoc during his lifetime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T08:20:24-08:00","id":60790,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all suggestions, especially mechanical ones. I recently got a new idea - to use Shadowrun setting but with no metahumans. Return of magic, awakening of plants and animals are results of hedge getting influence over real world. After many years people get used to them, rest almost as written. Basically, we get goblins and goblin fruits in real wold.<br /> <br /> Mages and Shamans could get something between Fae-Touched template and powers from Second Sight, Hunter groups would hunt more hostile goblin creatures, Changelings would try to protect hedge barrier from opening further. Insect spirits and Horrors can be treated as True Fae. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s just an idea for now. Need to think a little more about it.<br /> <br /> I probably will create something completely new after all as the setting, but considering ways to crossover Changeling with other Cyberpunk settings can give me some good ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T11:36:30-08:00","id":60943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/56099-cyberpunk-changeling?p=56116#post56116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do androids dream of electric sheep? If so, can a changeling visit those dreams, and maybe navigate from there into computer networks using something akin to the Skein? <b>Changeling</b> is uniquely situated to do things involving cyberpunk\u2019s traditional VR by drawing parallels between the Net and the Skein: e.g., the oneiromancy rules could easily be adapted to represent netrunning by treating the VR environments as if they were \u201cdreamscapes\u201d of computer systems . Blurring the boundaries between the two is in keeping with the notion that the line between man and machine is becoming blurred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The internet is a Promethean.<br /> <br /> food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:07:11-08:00","id":65850,"title":"","content":"This week at <b><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">my Facebook Changeling fan page</a></b>, I'll be looking at more technologically-minded Changeling elements. Feel free to stop by and have a look around. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T21:26:52-08:00","id":67700,"title":"","content":"So, long time Gibson fan, tried Shadowrun and hated it. Reckon nWoD is the best system for a cyber/biopunk game. I have been working on again off again on mods and translating them into nWoD rules. I use Hero Lab and have been hacking it for a while. I'm interested in working with some people in compiling a list of mods (cyber, bio and genetech) and then translating them into nWoD merits and or armour (things like dermal armour or genetic/bio skin moods to harden flesh seen to work better as armour rather than a merit). Is this the best place to find people interested in such work? More than happy to share the Hero Lab rules template once we're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2224-stephensaid","name":"stephensaid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}